f(g(x)) = f\left( \frac{-2}{x + 1} \right) = \frac{1 + \frac{-2}{x + 1}}{1 - \frac{-2}{x + 1}} = \frac{\frac{x - 1}{x + 1}}{\frac{x + 3}{x + 1}} = \frac{x - 1}{x + 3}
\] Next, we compute \( g(f(g(x))) \): \[
g(f(g(x))) = g\left( \frac{x - 1}{x + 3} \right) = \frac{-2}{\frac{x - 1}{x + 3} + 1} = \frac{-2}{\frac{x - 1 + x + 3}{x + 3}} = \frac{-2}{\frac{2x + 2}{x + 3}} = \frac{-2(x + 3)}{2(x + 1)} = \frac{-x - 3}{x + 1} = \frac{-(x + 1) - 2}{x + 1} = -1 - \frac{2}{x + 1}
\] This simplifies to \( g(f(g(x))) = -1 - \frac{2}{x + 1} = g(x) \). Thus, we can see that applying \( g \) after \( f \) results in the same function as \( g \) alone. Similarly, we can compute \( f(g(f(x))) \): \[
f(g(f(x))) = f\left( \frac{-2}{\frac{1 + x}{1 - x} + 1} \right) = f\left( \frac{-2}{\frac{1 + x + 1 - x}{1 - x}} \right) = f\left( \frac{-2}{\frac{2}{1 - x}} \right) = f(-(1 - x)) = f(x - 1) = \frac{1 + (x - 1)}{1 - (x - 1)} = \frac{x}{2 - x}
\] Finally, we can compute \( g(f(g(f(x)))) \): \[
g(f(g(f(x)))) = g\left( \frac{x}{2 - x} \right) = \frac{-2}{\frac{x}{2 - x} + 1} = \frac{-2}{\frac{x + 2 - x}{2 - x}} = \frac{-2}{\frac{2}{2 - x}} = - (2 - x) = x - 2
\] We can see that applying \( g \) after \( f \) and then \( f \) results in the function \( x - 2 \). This means that the nested function will eventually reduce to a simple linear function. Since we are applying \( f \) 8 times and \( g \) 8 times, alternating, we can see that the final function will be \( -1 \). So, applying \( g \) to \( -1 \) gives us: \[
